I haven't seen this particular trick pass through, so I thought I'd share.

Say you're wandering around looking at all the pretty statues and suddenly you
stumble into Medusa.  Fortunately she's still asleep, but unfortunately you
have no way to blind yourself.  Never fear; there's more than one way to skin a
Gorgon.  All you need is...

a mirror and speed (from boots, potion, or, if you're feeling lucky, intrinsic
speed).

What to do:  Stand next to Medusa and `a'pply the mirror.  Medusa will not turn
to stone at this point [the Dev Team's cagier than that :) ]; you will be
informed that "Medusa is tired and does not look in your mirror", and she will
now be awake.

IT IS VITALLY IMPORTANT THAT MEDUSA NOT ATTACK YOU AT THIS POINT.  If you have
speed, you can arrange for this to happen by applying the mirror in one of your
"extra" turns, when the other monsters don't move [you can try this with
intrinsic speed, but since your speed is less than twice normal, it's hard to
tell when you're going to get an extra move].

Now, on your next move, simply `a'pply the mirror again.  Medusa, being now
fully awake, will look in the mirror and get calcified.  No fuss, no muss.

